# Key correction first (important)

> **CORS does NOT always run after Spring Security.**

When you call:

```java
http.cors(cors -> {})
```

Spring Security **injects a CorsFilter at the *very beginning* of the Security filter chain**.

So the actual order becomes:

```
Request
 ↓
CorsFilter   ← (runs FIRST)
 ↓
Security filters (JWT, auth, etc.)
 ↓
Controller
```

This is the part most explanations get wrong.

